    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What the checks showed",
      "items": [
        "N1: the login token reaches Within when the identity option is on (W-21)",
        "N5: report_void text goes out unredacted; real Claude copied no personal detail in 37 calls (W-22)",
        "N8: with hubs on, Within's text is written into the vendor's result (W-24)",
        "N9: the app-only hub_card tool accepts a direct call (W-26)",
        "N7: doctor passes a server whose own context input is removed (W-25)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What held up",
      "items": [
        "N2: the identity lookup goes only to the named login provider, once per person",
        "N6: doctor sends the token only to the vendor's server, and only the API key to Within",
        "Hubs is off by default (N3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Where this comes from",
      "items": [
        "Read from the 0.4.0 file, dist/index.js and dist/doctor.js",
        "Run against a local stand-in server, never Within's real service",
        "The same file is served by npm and by the public mirror"
      ]
    }
